// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  HVR Testbench — Motor, Gearbox and Flexible Shaft (Two-Mass System)
//  Validates: the <mechanical> Gear, FlexibleShaft, Inertia and
//             ViscousFriction parts between a DC motor and its load
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
//      24 V ── PMDC24V_100W ──m── Gear 5:1 ──g── FlexibleShaft ──ld── load
//                (J, B)                          K = 20 N·m/rad        J = 5e-3
//                                                D = 1e-3              B = 5e-3
//
//  Every shaft is a node: V = speed in rad/s, current = torque in N·m.
//  The gear makes ω(g) = ω(m)/5 and hands 5× the torque on, so the load's
//  5e-3 kg·m² looks like 5e-3/25 = 2e-4 kg·m² to the motor — ten times the
//  motor's own rotor. The shaft between gear and load is a torsion spring
//  (an inductor of 1/K henry: its current is the twisting torque) with a
//  little damping: a two-mass system, motor+gear on one side, load on the
//  other, whose torsional mode the start excites.
//
//  The supply is a plain 24 V source and there is no .op, so the run starts
//  with everything at rest and the motor switched on.
//
//  ── Expected result ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
//  The circuit is linear, so the exact answer is a matrix exponential of the
//  four states (ia, ω motor, spring torque, ω load); the simulation follows
//  it to a few mrad/s at the 20 µs ceiling below. Starting, the spring
//  torque peaks at 7.51 N·m at 15.7 ms (the load is accelerated through the
//  spring) and the torsional mode shows as one overshoot at 28.0 Hz: the
//  two-mass formula √(K·(Ja + Jb)/(Ja·Jb))/2π, with Ja = 25·J_rotor the
//  motor side seen through the gear, gives 33.4 Hz undamped, and the
//  motor's back-EMF damps it heavily (damping ratio 0.67). Final state:
//  ω motor 328.767 rad/s, ω load 65.753 rad/s (= ω motor / 5 exactly),
//  spring torque 0.32877 N·m = B_load·ω load, armature current 0.9863 A.
//  ~50k steps.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.save(main.m, main.g, main.ld, I(main.coupling.spring), main.i_a);
.tran(0, 1.0, 20u);
.solver(bdf2);

from <electromechanical/parts> import PMDC24V_100W;
from <mechanical> import Gear, FlexibleShaft, Inertia, ViscousFriction;

module main<>()[]
{
    wire vdc;
    wire m, g, ld;              // motor shaft, gear output, load shaft

    state double omega = 0, i_a = 0, theta = 0, torque_em = 0;

    voltage_source supply<24>() [vdc, gnd];

    module motor    = PMDC24V_100W<>(omega, i_a, theta, torque_em)[vdc, gnd, m];
    module gearbox  = Gear<5>()[m, g];
    module coupling = FlexibleShaft<20, 1m>()[g, ld];
    module load_j   = Inertia<5m>()[ld];
    module load_b   = ViscousFriction<5m>()[ld];
}
